<title>INDIA: FII holdings hit limit in India SBI.</title>
<headline>FII holdings hit limit in India SBI.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign institutional investor (FII) holdings in State Bank of India (SBI), the country's biggest commercial bank, have reached the 20 percent ceiling, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Saturday.</p>
<p>&quot;No further purchases will be allowed in view of the condition stipulated by the government of India while approving their (SBI's) GDR (global depositary receipts) issue,&quot; the RBI said in a statement.</p>
<p>SBI had made a $400 million GDR issue in the second half 1996.</p>
<p>--Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
